{n}Jerribeth calls Serit into view. He stops just short of the table. She pushes the agreement toward him; he opens it, checks the signature, and folds it again with shaking fingers.{/n}
{n}He begins a grateful speech. She interrupts. It is impossible to mistake the impatience in her face, even without hearing her words.{/n}
