{n}By the time the pattern becomes clear, Soana is leaning heavily on her stick. You return to the cave for food and rest before finishing the comparison in the morning. The failed examination has cost you a day, but nobody needs to repeat it to make progress.{/n}

{n}Meret walks the route again, stopping where she rested with the sack. Sometimes she is certain; sometimes she argues with her own memory. You mark only the places she can identify by more than a familiar-looking tree.{/n}
{n}At two of them the moss beneath the sack has dried. At a third, bare stone shows no visible change. Soana pours one drop from the waterskin onto each patch, then watches without touching it.{/n}
