{n}You take a rubbing from the clean side, using the long stick to hold the cloth against the dangerous part. It is clumsier than working by hand, but the lines are legible.{/n}
{n}There is a clear strip beneath the hollow's lip. Soana marks it on the cloth. It may hold a temporary seal while you deal with the dish.{/n}
"I do not know who changed it," she says. "I do not intend to give the dead credit for every cruelty merely because the living have misplaced its author."

{n}Soana does not thank you for accepting her risk. She asks you to repeat your part in the working. You do so. Meret repeats hers, then asks where she should stand if the escape line has to be broken.{/n}
