{n}Soana gives her a grudging nod. Together you walk the proposed road, marking where the damp cord will lead the thing uphill and where the bare rock will stop it spreading farther.{/n}
{n}At the nursery, Soana cuts one low branch from a tree that stands directly in the way. She keeps the green piece tucked inside her sleeve. Neither of you asks her to explain it.{/n}

{n}Soana meets you before sunset. She has tied back her hair and fastened her sleeves close to her wrists. Meret carries the sack between two forked branches, keeping it clear of her clothing.{/n}
