{n}The clerk has treated every returning line as the beginning of a new verse. On the sheet, a repeated answer has become a command, and the second ford has been moved ahead of the first. You read the passages back in their probable order without pretending to restore the missing words.{/n}
{n}Runa sings against your reading. For the first time, the remembered route and the rhythm fit together. Vesk sits down.{/n}
