{n}It goes between you. There is not much room between you, and it finds it, and buries itself a finger's depth in the wooden pillar behind your two stools with a noise like a door being knocked on, once.{/n}
{n}Nobody is touched. The knife hums in the wood. Across the room the cook is staring at his empty hand.{/n}
{n}Mielarah looks at the knife, and at the space between you, and then, very slowly, at you.{/n}

