{n}The man who comes over from the door has to duck under the lintel of the Bad Luck and fold his wings to get through. A tiefling of the Midnight Isles, broad as a hatch cover, with a slaver's brand gone white on the side of his neck and a face that has been broken and set by amateurs more than once. He stops at a respectful distance from her. Everyone does.{/n}
